ralph/progress.txt:26770:  - **Static-test SECURITY.md substring assertions need the exact rendered substring, NOT a paraphrase**: the matcher checks `strings.Contains(text, want)` with the literal string. If the doc says `internal/release/...static_test.go` (with the path prefix), the substring `static_test.go` (without prefix) fails the contains check ONLY if the prefix is required by the assertion. Lesson: write the assertion list as the EXACT substrings the doc must contain, then write the doc to match. My first pass listed the full path `` `internal/release/rate_limit_bypass_resistance_static_test.go` `` but wrote the doc as a two-clause phrase that broke the substring; reworded the doc to keep the bare backtick-fenced filename `` `rate_limit_bypass_resistance_static_test.go` `` and added a "(under `internal/release/`, BE-0363)" follow-up — both halves now match independently.
