ralph/progress.txt:30049:- Added internal/controlplane/httpapi/environments_delete_contract_test.go closing the three contract-test criteria not directly asserted by environments_delete_test.go (BE-0160) or environments_delete_policy_test.go (BE-0162). Structural twin of environments_update_contract_test.go (BE-0158) and environments_get_contract_test.go (BE-0155), adapted to the DELETE single-environment shape: no JSON body, 202 Accepted success, EnvironmentDeleter port, action environment.delete, scheduled-deletion semantics rendered with a deletion_scheduled_at stamp and a version-pinned ETag header.
ralph/progress.txt:30052:  - TestDeleteEnvironmentRequestLogRedactsBearerToken: pinned both legs (success with RoleOwner, deny with Disabled=true) using a recognisable bearer credential `yk_live_supersecret_environments_delete_DEADBEEF0123456789`; asserts the credential is absent from both the structured log JSON and the response body. The deny-leg deleter errors if invoked, proving the leak axis is not "deleter rendered the bearer into an error string".
ralph/progress.txt:30070:  - The DELETE wire shape has no secret-bearing fields (display_name, slug, version, deletion_scheduled_at are all public), so the "marker absence in response body" assertion only needs to scan for the bearer credential — there is no need for an additional per-row marker over a secret-bearing field. Contrast: a future contract test for an endpoint that returns rendered environment variables (BE-0173 / BE-0176) would also need to seed a `RENDERED_VAR_MARKER` into the variable value and assert its absence from the response body for non-superuser principals.
ralph/progress.txt:31969:- Implemented: internal/controlplane/store/quota_policy_tenant_isolation_test.go — repository-layer tenant-isolation tests for the quota_policies table. quota_policies is a dual-scope table (plan_default OR organization) whose ONLY mutation surface is UpsertOrganizationPolicy and whose row body is only observable through the typed resolvers (EffectiveLimit / ListEffectiveLimits / ListOrganizationUsage). No per-id Get / Update / Delete surface exists, so the cross-tenant guarantee at this layer is exhaustively the projection invariant on every resolver leg AND the byte-identical-bystander invariant on the upsert. Coverage (9 tests): (1) EffectiveLimit per-resource is tenant-scoped — orgB's override does not appear when orgA queries the same resource; (2) ListEffectiveLimits rendered count is local to the queried tenant (orgA=1, orgB=3) — no count cross; (3) shared-resource isolation (both tenants override `projects` with distinct limit/mode — each sees its OWN); (4) plan isolation (orgA on 'starter' must not see 'pro' plan defaults); (5) ListOrganizationUsage is tenant scoped at BOTH the policies CTE and the usage CTE; (6) shared-counter isolation (both tenants have a quota_usage counter for the same resource with distinct used_value); (7) Upsert INSERT branch on orgA leaves orgB's bystander row byte-identical (the SAME resource on both tenants — the ON CONFLICT predicate is exercised); (8) Upsert UPDATE branch on orgA leaves orgB's bystander row byte-identical (both tenants pre-seeded with an override on the SAME resource — the maximally adversarial fixture for the partial-unique-index ON CONFLICT target); (9) same-resource upserts in two tenants both succeed (positive-direction pair for the bystander proofs — proves the partial unique index is per-tenant, not global).
ralph/progress.txt:32238:  - The deployments table stores NO secret-bearing column (source_ref is a branch/commit/tag/image name; error_message is redacted by the worker before persistence). The BE-0434-style raw-secret probe and the redaction-needle-in-error probe have no analogue here — but the BE-0458 acceptance criteria still apply structurally: rendered environment variable values, tokens, API keys and cookies do not appear on this table because they live in their own scoped tables.
