ralph/progress.txt:33332:  - The Complete cross-tenant test should embed a recognisable canary string ("forged":"orgA-tries-to-complete-orgB-claim") in the response_body argument so a future reader sees immediately what the test was protecting against. A bland `[]byte("body")` argument would obscure the worst-case shape ("orgA silently completes orgB's claim with arbitrary bytes"). The canary also doubles as a redaction-leak probe — if a future error-formatter regression embeds the rendered envelope in the typed Conflict's Error() / Message / Hint, the canary surfaces in a grep across the test output.
